# About Me
I'm an Electrical Engineer with a minor in Computer Science and extensive experience in industrial automation and control systems.
My professional background includes PLC programming, industrial networking, motor controls, VFDs, HMIs, and troubleshooting automation systems. I've worked with several industrial programming environments, including Ladder Logic, Function Block Diagram (FBD), and Structured Text (IEC 61131-3), including platforms such as CODESYS.
I studied several programming languages in college, but most of my programming experience since then has been focused on industrial automation, with some hobby projects using Arduino.
I'm generally more comfortable reading and understanding code than writing it from scratch, primarily because I don't regularly work with traditional programming languages or their syntax.

## Currently Learning
- Python 
- C++ (Arduino)
- Git and GitHub
- Improving my coding skills through regular practice
- Expanding my programming knowledge beyond industrial automation

## My Goal
I'm using GitHub to become more familiar with modern software development tools, improve my programming skills, and explore projects outside of my day-to-day industrial automation work.
